GNU assembler 2.43 for Belka
============================

The upstream release and SHA-256 are pinned in tools/toolchain/sources.
The source remains in the build cache, with its original GPL notices.
The patch here recognises Belka in config.sub/config.guess and selects
the existing amd64 ELF BFD and GNU assembler backends. GNU ld is disabled;
Belka continues to use its illumos link-editor and archive tools.

The optional native-object-tools target also builds objcopy, objdump,
readelf, size, strings and strip for compiler bootstrap and object
inspection. It retains illumos ld, ar, nm and the ranlib adapter. GNU strip
is used on relocatable bootstrap objects; the image builder leaves dynamic
illumos executables unstripped.
